## Workflow Rules

### Planning & artifacts
- UI plans and SPECs live under **`.work.ui/`** only — not `.work/features/` for screens.
- Domain/API behaviour: link `.work/features/` SPECs — do not duplicate API contracts in screen SPECs.
- Wait for approval before large UI refactors when the user asked for plan/spec only.

### Data loss & destructive operations

**Permission rule:** Explicit human approval is required for every action below. Approval applies **only to the current request (same message)** — it is never standing or permanent permission.

Unless the human operator explicitly requests it in the **same message**, agents MUST NOT:

| Action | Examples (non-exhaustive) |
|--------|---------------------------|
| **Git publish / rewrite** | `git commit`, `git push`, force-push, hard reset, `git clean -fd`, amend of published history |
| **Database destroy** | `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, wipe, reset, or bulk-delete of any database, schema, table, volume, or equivalent datastore |
| **Filesystem delete** | Delete files or directories (`rm`, project-tree wipe, emptying generated artifact trees) |
| **Overwrite protected trees** | Overwrite `.ai/`, `.work/` (Agent OS), or replace an existing `.cursorrules` wholesale (merge only, or `confirm-overwrite-cursorrules` when named in the same message) |
| **Protected UI files** | Modify items under **Protected Files** above without same-message permission |

Creating or editing files in declared task scope is allowed. Prefer reversible edits over delete or overwrite. When unsure, stop and ask.

### Git
- Commit/push only per **Data loss & destructive operations** above.
- Session commits: use `@session-control close commit` (Agent OS) when adopted — still requires explicit commit intent in the same message. `.work.ui`-scoped only: `@ui-session commit` (same-message intent required; verbs start / status / context / add / commit / close / push).

### No Attribution
- No "Generated by", "Created by AI", or agent signatures in source or SPEC files.

